\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. With joy we meditate the grace
\par Of our High-priest above;
\par His heart is made of tenderness,
\par And ever yearns with love.
\par 
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Touched with a sympathy within,
\par He knows our feeble frame;
\par He knows what sore temptations mean,
\par For He hath felt the same.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. He in the days of feeble flesh
\par Poured out His cries and tears;
\par And, though exalted, feels afresh
\par What every member bears.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. He'll never quench the smoking flax,
\par But raise it to a flame;
\par The bruised reed He never breaks;
\par Nor scorns the meanest name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Then let our humble faith address
\par His mercy and His power:
\par We shall obtain delivering grace
\par In the distressing hour.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

